Z||000000||reddog||09-22-2001||12:09 AM||||I have an 86 GT w/auto transmission and there seems to be a loud thumping noise coming from the left rear wheel.It seems to be louder when I turn to the right and stops when I apply the brakes. Only noticable on decelaration or coasting at low speed. Rear brakes are in need of changing and parking brake does not engage fully. Is this a cv joint problem/ suspension or could it be in the brakes?<P>Also I have a very loud clicking sound coming from the right side of the engine compartment when I have the a/c or the defrost on. However the noise stops if I turn the a/c off or put the controls on vent.Also,I am having a hell of a time with belts squealing. I had both belts changes about four months ago and have tighted them on three separate occasions but they still squeal! Lastly I replaced a muffler that had a large hole blown out of the top when I first bought the car about 5 months ago. I've noticed that after accelarating when I let off of the throttle and coast there is a low popping noise in the exhaust that sounds like popcorn popping. What causes this and how can I fix it! Help would be deeply appreciated!!!    ||||reg||1
Z||000001||dennis_6||09-22-2001||04:45 AM||||I doubt you have this problem but I got about the same car as yours except mine is a notchback.  I had a leaking coldstart injector and the fuel was somehow igniting.  Worth checking.  Make sure there is no fuel puddles under your coldstart!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||09-22-2001||02:10 PM||||The noise from the wheel could be a combination of breaks CV and even the bearing unit. Also posible the ball joint or tierod is sloppy.<P>hard to say about the motor. <P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/halfpole.gif"> <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
